---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SystemDiagram from '../components/diagrams/SystemDiagram.astro';
import {MODEL_SPECS} from '../data/model-specs';
import {SITE_URL} from '../config/site';
const steps=[
['01','Understand your outage needs','Decide what must stay powered and how long your typical outage lasts.','/guides/first-time-buyer-guide/'],
['02','Build your load profile','Record real nameplate loads and motor-starting requirements before choosing a kW number.','/planning/sizing/'],
['03','Plan generator capacity','Compare essential-load, unmanaged and load-managed scenarios without hiding unknowns.','/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/'],
['04','Compare brands','Narrow the field by documented product families, warranty terms and local service questions.','/brands/'],
['05','Compare exact models','Check fuel-specific output, transfer equipment, documentation and evidence gaps.','/models/'],
['06','Understand installed cost','Separate the generator from site work, fuel, electrical, permits and commissioning.','/cost/standby-generator-cost/'],
['07','Choose a fuel path','Compare natural gas and propane around availability, storage, consumption and outage resilience.','/guides/natural-gas-vs-propane/'],
['08','Plan the installation','Check placement, transfer equipment, local approvals and qualified-trade responsibilities.','/installation/'],
['09','Normalize installer quotes','Make missing scope, exclusions and apples-to-oranges differences visible before comparing totals.','/planning/quotes/'],
['10','Verify serviceability','Confirm who commissions, maintains and supports the exact system before you sign.','/research/local-service/']
];
const trust=[
['Exact-model research','Fuel-specific ratings and package variants stay attached to exact configurations.'],
['Primary-source evidence','Manufacturer manuals and official sources are identified where available.'],
['Unknowns stay unknown','Conflicts and missing evidence are shown instead of silently filled in.'],
['No invented testing','Desk research is never presented as hands-on testing or licensed trade review.']
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Whole House Generator Guide: Sizing, Cost & Installation" description="Independent whole house generator research for US homeowners covering sizing, installed cost, brands, fuel, installation, exact models and quote comparison." schema={{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebSite',name:'HomeGeneratorGuide',url:SITE_URL+'/'}}>
<section class="premium-home-hero">
  <div class="editorial-container premium-hero-grid">
    <div class="premium-hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT STANDBY-GENERATOR RESEARCH · US HOMEOWNERS</p>
      <h1>Choose a whole house generator before the sales conversation.</h1>
      <p class="premium-hero-lede">Buying a whole house generator? Compare load-based sizing, real installed-cost scope, exact standby models and installer quotes before committing to a major backup-power project.</p>
      <div class="premium-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/planning/sizing/">Build my load plan →</a><a class="premium-text-link" href="/planning/quotes/">Already have quotes? Compare them →</a></div>
      <div class="premium-proof-line" aria-label="Editorial standards"><span>Independent methodology</span><span>Source verification dates</span><span>No sponsored rankings</span></div>
    </div>
    <figure class="premium-hero-visual">
      <img src="/images/user-editorial/premium-home-at-dusk.webp" width="1536" height="1037" alt="American home at dusk with a residential standby generator near the exterior wall" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
      <figcaption><strong>Research the whole system.</strong> Generator, transfer equipment, fuel, site work, permits, commissioning and service all shape the final decision.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="editorial-container py-9 sm:py-14" aria-labelledby="quick-start-heading">
  <div class="mb-6">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE 60-SECOND START</p>
    <h2 id="quick-start-heading" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-primary sm:text-3xl">Three questions before you choose a generator</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-gray-700">You do not need to understand every generator specification today. Start with the answer you need; move into exact-model evidence only when you are ready.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-[#cbd5cf] bg-[#f4f8f5] p-5 sm:p-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#315647]">01 · SIZE</p>
      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-primary">What size do I need?</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Plan the circuits that matter and record real equipment loads. Square footage alone is not a sizing method.</p>
      <a class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center font-bold text-primary underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4" href="/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/">Start with sizing →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-[#cbd5cf] bg-[#f4f8f5] p-5 sm:p-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#315647]">02 · COST</p>
      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-primary">How much will it cost?</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Understand equipment versus installed price, site work, gas and electrical scope before comparing bids.</p>
      <a class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center font-bold text-primary underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4" href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/">See installed cost factors →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-[#cbd5cf] bg-[#f4f8f5] p-5 sm:p-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#315647]">03 · CHOOSE</p>
      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-primary">Which model fits my home?</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Compare exact fuel ratings, switch packages, warranty documents and who will service it locally.</p>
      <a class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center font-bold text-primary underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4" href="/comparisons/five-brand-standby-generator-comparison/">Compare five brands →</a>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-600">Already have competing bids? <a class="font-semibold text-primary underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4" href="/planning/quotes/">Compare three installer quotes side by side →</a></p>
</section>

<section class="editorial-container py-10 sm:py-14" aria-labelledby="research-topics-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">START WITH YOUR QUESTION</p>
  <h2 id="research-topics-heading" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-primary sm:text-3xl">Whole house generator research, in decision order</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-gray-600">Find the cost of a whole house generator, compare generator brands and sizing options, or understand what installation involves. These are educational guides—not installer listings or claims of hands-on testing.</p>
  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Whole house generator cost →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Equipment prices, installed-price ranges and what changes a quote.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Whole house generator sizing →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Running loads, motor starts, fuel ratings and load-management choices.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/installation/what-to-expect/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Whole house generator installation →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Assessment, transfer equipment, permits, fuel work and commissioning.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/comparisons/five-brand-standby-generator-comparison/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Best whole house generator? →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Compare five brands by exact-model evidence, local service and system fit.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/comparisons/generac-vs-kohler/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Generac vs. Kohler →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Two 26 kW-class configurations, fuel-specific output and ATS scope.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/brands/kohler/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Kohler whole house generators →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Compare documented 26RCA/26RCAL packages, ratings and warranty terms.</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="premium-trust-strip" aria-labelledby="trust-title"><div class="editorial-container"><div class="premium-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">WHY TRUST THE RESEARCH</p><h2 id="trust-title">Evidence first. Confidence second.</h2><p>We distinguish manufacturer facts, planning assumptions, editorial interpretation and unresolved evidence.</p></div><div class="premium-trust-grid">{trust.map(([title,body])=><article><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div><p class="premium-method-note"><strong>{MODEL_SPECS.length} exact configurations</strong> currently tracked, including package variants. Research-based guidance; no hands-on generator testing. Technical professional review remains pending. <a href="/review-process/">Read the review process →</a></p></div></section>

<section class="editorial-container premium-journey" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
  <div class="premium-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE HOMEOWNER DECISION PATH</p><h2 id="journey-title">Ready to go deeper? The full 10-step checklist.</h2><p>Do not start with a logo or a headline kW rating. Move through the project in the order that reduces expensive surprises.</p></div>
  <ol class="premium-journey-list">{steps.map(([n,title,description,href])=><li><a href={href}><span class="premium-step-number" aria-hidden="true">{n}</span><span><strong>{title}</strong><small>{description}</small></span><span class="premium-step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li>)}</ol>
</section>

<section class="premium-system-band"><div class="editorial-container premium-system-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">SEE THE SYSTEM</p><h2>A standby generator is not just a box beside the house.</h2><p>Utility power, transfer equipment, the electrical panel, selected loads, fuel capacity and load management work as one system. Understanding those relationships makes model and quote comparisons far more useful.</p><ul class="premium-link-list"><li><a href="/installation/automatic-transfer-switch-guide/">How the automatic transfer switch works →</a></li><li><a href="/sizing/generator-load-management/">How load management changes sizing →</a></li><li><a href="/sizing/whole-home-vs-essential-loads/">Whole-home vs essential-load backup →</a></li></ul></div><div class="premium-diagram-shell"><SystemDiagram/><p>Conceptual system explainer. Installation details depend on the equipment, property, manufacturer instructions and local requirements.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="editorial-container premium-feature-grid" aria-label="Research tools">
  <article class="premium-feature premium-feature-image"><img src="/images/sizing-electrician-panel.webp" width="720" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Electrician evaluating a residential electrical panel for generator planning" /><div><p class="eyebrow">SIZE WITH CONTEXT</p><h2>Build the load plan before choosing capacity.</h2><p>Work through heating, cooling, pumps, kitchen, laundry and special loads. Unknown inputs remain explicit so a planning estimate does not masquerade as a measured home load.</p><a class="button" href="/planning/sizing/">Start guided sizing →</a></div></article>
  <article class="premium-feature premium-feature-image"><img src="/images/cost-install-quote.webp" width="720" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Homeowner reviewing an itemized standby generator installation proposal" /><div><p class="eyebrow">THE QUOTE DESK</p><h2>Compare scope, not just totals.</h2><p>Normalize generator, ATS, fuel, electrical, site work, permits, commissioning, warranty, maintenance, taxes and exclusions across three proposals.</p><a class="button" href="/planning/quotes/">Compare installer quotes →</a></div></article>
</section>

<section class="premium-final-cta"><div class="editorial-container"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU SIGN</p><h2>Turn research into questions your installer must answer.</h2><p>Bring the same load assumptions, exact equipment identifiers and scope checklist to every proposal. That is how a homeowner gets a cleaner comparison.</p></div><div class="premium-final-actions"><a class="button" href="/cost/standby-generator-quote-checklist/">Open the quote checklist →</a><a href="/models/">Browse exact model research</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>